// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO7/35-37/39/40/45 - dedicated onboard TFT
// display + SPI bus, GPIO21/34 - internal power-gate lines. Confirmed via
// vendor pins_arduino.h (TFT_CS=7,MOSI=35,SCK=36,MISO=37,TFT_DC=39,
// TFT_RST=40,TFT_BACKLITE=45,TFT_I2C_POWER=21,NEOPIXEL_POWER=34):
// https://github.com/espressif/arduino-esp32/blob/master/variants/adafruit_feather_esp32s2_tft/pins_arduino.h
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO13 tagged "led_high" - confirmed active-high user
// LED (LED_BUILTIN=13; same circuit/labeling across the Feather
// ESP32-Sx line, see https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-esp32-s2-feather/pinouts).
// GPIO33 tagged "led_neopixel" - confirmed onboard NeoPixel
// (PIN_NEOPIXEL=33, same pins_arduino.h).
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO0 tagged "button" - confirmed onboard BOOT
// pushbutton, documented as usable in application code:
// https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-esp32-s2-tft-feather/read-a-push-button
// - "The ESP32-S2 TFT Feather's push button ... is located directly next
// to the TFT" and labeled "BOOT".
